WEBVTT


00:01:36.357 --> 00:01:37.491
No potty breaks.


00:01:37.958 --> 00:01:42.462
Dude, stop the truck.
You can leave us here. It's fine.


00:02:03.092 --> 00:02:04.760
Hey, how far is the lake?


00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:06.224
About a mile east.


00:02:06.658 --> 00:02:09.327
Perfect, because l need a bath.


00:02:25.424 --> 00:02:29.494
Not that l don't love this sexy,
impulsive thing, 'cause l do.


00:02:29.958 --> 00:02:32.827
But what are the chances
we're gonna get lost


00:02:32.925 --> 00:02:36.728
and, you know, we're gonna die horribly?


00:02:37.858 --> 00:02:41.895
Look, you keep talking like that
and you're gonna start lactating.


00:03:00.658 --> 00:03:02.926
Wow. It's so beautiful here.


00:03:06.058 --> 00:03:07.692
And real scary, huh?


00:03:08.458 --> 00:03:09.458
Okay, fine.


00:03:09.991 --> 00:03:11.692
Make fun of me.


00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:16.428
But when a Wolverine comes out
and mauls you, you're gonna be sorry.


00:03:17.391 --> 00:03:18.992
And you're naked.


00:03:19.591 --> 00:03:20.892
You noticed.


00:03:24.424 --> 00:03:25.458
God.


00:03:34.324 --> 00:03:35.758
What are you laughing at, pal?
l meant to do that.


00:03:40.124 --> 00:03:41.391
Come on.


00:03:41.491 --> 00:03:43.492
-You laughing at me?
-Yeah.


00:03:44.058 --> 00:03:45.592
Are you? l see.


00:03:49.291 --> 00:03:50.325
Hey, what's that?


00:03:50.791 --> 00:03:53.326
Come on, the water's cold. It shrinks a bit.


00:03:56.524 --> 00:03:58.626
What? l don't hear anything.


00:04:00.658 --> 00:04:04.094
-Hey, come on. l got an idea.
-Cool.


00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:20.925
God, something bit me.


00:04:21.257 --> 00:04:23.125
Yeah, right. Perhaps Wolverine.


00:04:30.191 --> 00:04:32.226
l've never heard you be so verbal.


00:04:33.191 --> 00:04:34.659
Take it easy, cowboy.


00:04:37.257 --> 00:04:39.559
Now, you see,
that's what l've been talking about.


00:04:44.458 --> 00:04:45.492
Help!


00:04:47.858 --> 00:04:48.858
Help!


00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:53.891
Oh, my God!


00:05:38.591 --> 00:05:40.993
Hey, big guy. You wanna come inside?


00:05:41.257 --> 00:05:42.324
Your mom needs some help.


00:05:42.458 --> 00:05:44.059
-Sure, Dad.
-Okay.


00:05:56.891 --> 00:05:58.025
Sadie!


00:06:22.025 --> 00:06:25.695
No cell phone reception.
It's like we've gone back in time.


00:06:26.991 --> 00:06:30.594
How can this place smell of cookies
and foot cream simultaneously?


00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:33.659
Well, they were
two of Aunt Sadie's favorite things.


00:06:33.791 --> 00:06:35.792
That and dropping F-bombs.


00:06:37.025 --> 00:06:39.727
l am not gonna miss that at Thanksgiving.


00:06:39.825 --> 00:06:42.794
-Didn't she always blame it on the dog?
-Yeah.


00:06:43.991 --> 00:06:49.262
You know, as both your wife
and your real estate agent,


00:06:50.424 --> 00:06:55.295
l can pretty much say with confidence
that most of this crap has gotta go.


00:06:59.058 --> 00:07:00.759
lt's gonna be a huge job.


00:07:00.858 --> 00:07:04.161
Yeah, but we can't bring it all back
to the house.


00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:08.125
She was eccentric.


00:07:08.858 --> 00:07:10.059
Really?


00:07:10.624 --> 00:07:13.560
Yeah, a different word
popped into my mind.


00:07:17.025 --> 00:07:20.261
You know, everything's almost exactly
how l remember it.


00:07:20.357 --> 00:07:22.325
l mean, l never thought that...


00:07:22.691 --> 00:07:25.026
Well, l never thought
that we'd be cleaning out her cabin, so...


00:07:27.357 --> 00:07:30.460
l feel like l'm selling part of my childhood
with this place.


00:07:30.558 --> 00:07:33.627
l know, honey. But it's best we stay in town.


00:07:35.891 --> 00:07:37.425
-Can l have that?
-No.


00:07:40.391 --> 00:07:41.492
-Yeah, sure.
-No.


00:07:41.624 --> 00:07:42.591
-Yeah.
-Yes.


00:07:49.191 --> 00:07:53.495
l have a pop quiz for you,
Mr. EPA Scientist. Okay?


00:07:54.058 --> 00:07:58.162
So what kind of animal
lives in a tank like that one?


00:08:00.825 --> 00:08:02.159
The smart money's on that lizard right there.


00:08:02.257 --> 00:08:03.558
-What?
-ls there nothing there?


00:08:03.658 --> 00:08:05.126
Well, that was probably my mistake,
l thought it was...


00:08:05.558 --> 00:08:06.825
Funny!


00:08:06.925 --> 00:08:08.660
Freak out the city girl.


00:08:08.758 --> 00:08:11.427
Just 'cause l don't share
the Bickerman infatuation with...


00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:14.226
What? Life? Nature?


00:08:14.324 --> 00:08:17.126
Nature to you. Disgusting creatures to me.


00:08:17.925 --> 00:08:19.359
All right, well, heads up for both of you,


00:08:19.458 --> 00:08:22.093
there might be an escaped lizard
somewhere in the house.


00:08:22.191 --> 00:08:23.825
Can we keep it?


00:08:23.925 --> 00:08:27.361
Absolutely not. No.
Besides, you already have a pet.


00:08:27.458 --> 00:08:28.792
Crocodiles aren't pets.


00:08:28.891 --> 00:08:29.992
Well, they are to some people, pal.


00:08:30.257 --> 00:08:31.291
Not if they're stuffed.


00:08:31.424 --> 00:08:32.458
You know what?


00:08:32.858 --> 00:08:37.596
lf we find any kind of vermin in the house,
your dad is gonna take care of it.


00:08:39.558 --> 00:08:40.592
Dad?


00:08:40.691 --> 00:08:43.994
ln a completely humane way, of course.


00:08:44.324 --> 00:08:45.458
Sure. Sit down.


00:09:06.424 --> 00:09:09.593
-Mr. Bickerman?
-Hey, Nate. Nathan. Come on in.


00:09:14.391 --> 00:09:15.425
Sheriff Willinger.


00:09:15.524 --> 00:09:17.125
-Hey. Susan.
-Hey.


00:09:17.224 --> 00:09:18.858
lt's been a while.


00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:21.160
Almost a year since Sadie passed.


00:09:21.257 --> 00:09:22.524
l was going by, l saw your vehicle.


00:09:22.858 --> 00:09:24.793
l thought l'd drop in and say hey.


00:09:24.891 --> 00:09:25.992
-Yeah, of course.
-Yeah.


00:09:26.925 --> 00:09:27.959
Takes after Sadie, huh?


00:09:29.458 --> 00:09:32.527
Connor, could you give us a minute, please?


00:09:32.791 --> 00:09:34.192
-Okay.
-Thanks.


00:09:36.025 --> 00:09:38.293
Yeah, we haven't told him, so...


00:09:41.858 --> 00:09:42.858
l don't blame you.


00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:45.527
A boy his age, that would raise questions
you don't have answers to.


00:09:46.658 --> 00:09:49.227
Hell, l'd like to know what your aunt
was doing feeding wild crocs.


00:09:49.758 --> 00:09:52.327
Well, she was lonely.


00:09:53.324 --> 00:09:54.925
l mean, l know we live in town.


00:09:55.025 --> 00:09:57.127
We don't get out here that much. And with...


00:09:57.224 --> 00:09:59.059
You know, ever since Connor was born,
and our jobs, it's...


00:09:59.157 --> 00:10:00.224
Well, there's never enough time.


00:10:01.224 --> 00:10:02.858
And now the place is for sale.


00:10:04.791 --> 00:10:08.728
lt took a year for us to drive out here
to clean up Sadie's stuff. It's...


00:10:08.825 --> 00:10:11.994
You know, believe me,
this isn't easy for me. We...


00:10:12.092 --> 00:10:14.761
lf we had a choice,
we probably wouldn't even sell it.


00:10:14.858 --> 00:10:17.927
Yeah, but it's not like we can come out here
and have a picnic


00:10:18.025 --> 00:10:19.159
and forget about what happened.


00:10:19.257 --> 00:10:21.926
l don't even like bringing Connor here
for a few hours.


00:10:22.324 --> 00:10:24.559
Well, that's understandable.


00:10:24.658 --> 00:10:28.661
l'd like you to know
that l've been all over that lake.


00:10:28.758 --> 00:10:31.827
Back to front, top to bottom,
had a sonar rig brought in.


00:10:31.925 --> 00:10:35.495
l can tell you, ma'am, there ain't nothing
swimming in that lake bigger than a trout.


00:10:35.591 --> 00:10:37.459
Yeah, but you can never be sure.


00:10:37.558 --> 00:10:41.862
-Right?
-Ma'am, when my predecessor left the job,


00:10:41.958 --> 00:10:43.959
-the county wanted to hire somebody...
-Hey, where are you going?


00:10:44.058 --> 00:10:45.692
...who could guarantee
that what happened here


00:10:45.791 --> 00:10:47.392
didn't happen again, and that's me.


00:10:47.491 --> 00:10:48.859
Now, you're gonna have to trust me.


00:10:49.791 --> 00:10:52.860
You know? l've seen things that are
a lot worse than what happened here.


00:10:52.958 --> 00:10:57.095
Hell, l had a 6'5'' cross-dresser
come at me with a machete.


00:11:00.691 --> 00:11:02.526
What l'm trying to say is,


00:11:03.424 --> 00:11:06.994
in this world it's the people
you gotta worry about, not the animals.


00:11:07.291 --> 00:11:09.059
-l'm gonna be on my way, here.
-Sure, sure.


00:11:09.157 --> 00:11:10.191
Thank you for coming by.


00:11:11.691 --> 00:11:13.325
You take care, now.


00:11:34.357 --> 00:11:38.060
All l'm saying is that if the lake is cleared,
there's no reason to sell.


00:11:38.157 --> 00:11:41.260
Nathan, we didn't even come here
when Sadie was alive.


00:11:41.357 --> 00:11:45.094
l know. But, l mean, no one knows better
than you how bad the market is right now.


00:11:45.191 --> 00:11:47.393
l'm just saying, why don't we wait?


00:11:47.491 --> 00:11:49.860
You know, test it out. We could... Please?


00:11:51.958 --> 00:11:55.361
You know what? Fine. Okay.
We can wait until the market recovers.


00:11:55.458 --> 00:11:58.227
-But Connor is not swimming in that lake.
-Done.


00:11:58.324 --> 00:11:59.291
But he's not gonna make any friends


00:11:59.391 --> 00:12:01.659
if we keep dragging him off
to the middle of nowhere.


00:12:01.791 --> 00:12:02.825
Well...


00:12:03.025 --> 00:12:04.192
Connor?


00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:08.226
-Where'd he go?
-l don't know.


00:12:10.491 --> 00:12:13.460
Come here, little guy.
l'm not gonna hurt you.


00:12:45.224 --> 00:12:48.293
Looks like l got a pet after all. Lots of them.


00:12:50.958 --> 00:12:53.493
Connor! Don't run off
without telling us, okay?


00:12:53.591 --> 00:12:55.159
-Sorry.
-Come on.


00:12:55.257 --> 00:12:57.292
We're driving back to town.


00:13:16.157 --> 00:13:17.992
lt's 6:00 a.m. and you're not on the trail.


00:13:18.092 --> 00:13:20.294
-You going soft on me?
-Yeah.


00:13:20.391 --> 00:13:22.860
-l thought you had a big day.
-l do.


00:13:24.124 --> 00:13:26.826
Don't l at least get a ''good morning''?


00:13:26.958 --> 00:13:29.560
Sorry. We lost another one.


00:13:30.958 --> 00:13:33.360
The signal from the elk's radio collar
went and became erratic,


00:13:33.458 --> 00:13:36.494
and then we lost it completely
yesterday afternoon, so...


00:13:36.591 --> 00:13:38.192
This one is gonna be the last one.


00:13:38.291 --> 00:13:40.426
Meaning you know
what's been happening to them?


00:13:40.524 --> 00:13:41.625
l think it's a poacher.


00:13:42.357 --> 00:13:45.259
l think they're bringing hunters
onto state land. l think it's a business.


00:13:45.357 --> 00:13:46.491
And...


00:13:49.691 --> 00:13:52.060
l hope you find your bad guy.


00:13:54.058 --> 00:13:55.092
Good morning.


00:13:55.191 --> 00:13:59.061
And don't forget to say goodbye
to your zoologist-in-training.


00:13:59.157 --> 00:14:02.026
Right. Right. Hey, is Vica coming by today?


00:14:03.124 --> 00:14:04.859
She has to take her dog to the vet.


00:14:04.958 --> 00:14:07.093
Something about
it having another panic attack,


00:14:07.191 --> 00:14:10.961
but l promised Connor
l would spend the day with him anyway, so...


00:14:11.058 --> 00:14:13.593
Hey, Connor, l'm heading out the door.


00:14:13.691 --> 00:14:17.027
You wanna say goodbye to me
before l leave? Love you.


00:14:17.791 --> 00:14:21.694
-Goodbye? When did you get back?
-Late last night. Something came up at work


00:14:21.825 --> 00:14:25.028
and l will tell you all about it
when l get home, okay?


00:14:25.124 --> 00:14:27.526
-But, Dad...
-Hey, l got to go, okay?


00:14:29.624 --> 00:14:30.658
Bye.


00:15:04.458 --> 00:15:08.562
God! Mother of...
Next year, you are going to summer school.


00:15:09.558 --> 00:15:13.428
You've been on there all morning.
When are you gonna be done?


00:15:13.524 --> 00:15:16.226
Soon, honey. There are a lot of cabins
that need renting


00:15:16.324 --> 00:15:19.093
and l have so many people counting on me.


00:15:22.357 --> 00:15:24.726
Two hours, tops, okay? l promise.


00:15:28.324 --> 00:15:31.126
Honey, why don't you just go play outside?


00:15:32.558 --> 00:15:33.725
Connor?


00:15:49.724 --> 00:15:50.791
Hey, guys.


00:15:52.025 --> 00:15:53.793
Hey, guys.
Do you wanna see something cool?


00:15:54.724 --> 00:15:57.560
''Hey, guys. Wanna see something cool?''


00:16:00.925 --> 00:16:03.894
-What a freaking jester.
-What a dork.


00:16:16.224 --> 00:16:17.658
Feeding time.


00:16:45.724 --> 00:16:46.791
That's all l got.


00:16:49.858 --> 00:16:51.759
Hey, no eating the cook.


00:16:52.458 --> 00:16:54.126
l'll try to bring more next time.


00:17:13.357 --> 00:17:14.725
Where is it?


00:17:15.524 --> 00:17:18.393
Around back. Tried to take a chunk
out of one of my customers.


00:17:18.491 --> 00:17:20.426
lt's wicked big.


00:17:26.124 --> 00:17:27.959
l think he came up through the toilet.


00:17:38.058 --> 00:17:39.926
You're wasting my time.


00:17:40.825 --> 00:17:42.226
Take it easy, Tony.


00:17:45.157 --> 00:17:46.424
Willinger.


00:17:48.491 --> 00:17:49.792
Yes, dear.


00:17:52.958 --> 00:17:54.793
Yes, dear. Yeah. Yeah.


00:17:56.157 --> 00:17:58.425
Here, could you hold on? Hold on, dear.


00:17:59.724 --> 00:18:01.025
Willinger.


00:18:01.357 --> 00:18:02.958
l got a lead on my missing elk.


00:18:03.058 --> 00:18:05.326
Seems she's wandering around
somewhere near Sadie's lake.


00:18:05.724 --> 00:18:08.159
Nathan, l don't wanna hear anything
about crocodiles.


00:18:08.257 --> 00:18:12.194
There's nothing in that lake
bigger than a trout. Just stay put.


00:18:15.058 --> 00:18:16.859
That was productive.


00:18:18.058 --> 00:18:19.359
Yes, dear.


00:18:23.357 --> 00:18:25.158
Well, you shouldn't have put it
in the microwave.


00:18:46.491 --> 00:18:47.959
I wish I could believe you.


00:18:48.758 --> 00:18:51.093
lt was a one-night stand, Marsha.
She meant nothing to me.


00:18:51.191 --> 00:18:52.992
-l have absolutely no feelings for her.
-But this is how...


00:18:53.092 --> 00:18:55.894
He was kissing Jessica
before the last commercial.


00:18:55.991 --> 00:18:59.794
...Susan's little one? The little one
with the same hair and eyes as yours.


00:19:00.058 --> 00:19:03.327
Susan? Susan means
absolutely nothing to me.


00:19:04.058 --> 00:19:05.526
Where's my mom?


00:19:05.624 --> 00:19:07.092
Connor, where have you been?


00:19:07.191 --> 00:19:08.292
Forgot my phone.


00:19:09.424 --> 00:19:10.858
Where are you going?


00:19:10.958 --> 00:19:14.928
Honey, l am so sorry, but l have a thing.


00:19:18.658 --> 00:19:19.925
What was l saying?


00:19:20.025 --> 00:19:21.693
l have a last minute open house.


00:19:22.724 --> 00:19:25.259
So l am gonna leave you with Vica
for the rest of the day


00:19:25.357 --> 00:19:27.726
and tomorrow we will go see a movie.
l promise.


00:19:27.825 --> 00:19:28.792
But you said that we'd...


00:19:28.891 --> 00:19:30.759
Connor, this is important.
Please understand.


00:19:30.891 --> 00:19:32.525
But l need to show you something.


00:19:32.925 --> 00:19:33.959
Well, show me when l get home,


00:19:34.991 --> 00:19:36.559
l love you so much.


00:19:36.658 --> 00:19:37.692
Bye.


00:19:57.491 --> 00:19:59.292
Connor! What are you doing?


00:19:59.958 --> 00:20:03.628
You smell like dead goat. Go take bath.


00:20:04.191 --> 00:20:08.395
l'm going to the store
to get some baseball cards.


00:20:09.491 --> 00:20:11.659
l don't care about your baseball cards.


00:20:22.424 --> 00:20:24.993
Connor! You didn't take bath.


00:21:27.092 --> 00:21:29.093
You got to stay away
from those cookies, boy.


00:21:29.825 --> 00:21:33.395
You seem to have gained
quite a bit of weight since l last saw you.


00:21:33.591 --> 00:21:35.960
About two minutes ago.


00:21:36.191 --> 00:21:37.325
Well, l...


00:21:38.291 --> 00:21:40.726
lf it were me, l'd kick your little butt.


00:21:41.891 --> 00:21:45.027
Parents' number.
And not the fake one, either.


00:21:49.025 --> 00:21:51.193
Gotta be out here somewhere.


00:21:59.991 --> 00:22:00.991
God!


00:22:01.092 --> 00:22:02.359
Sorry. Sorry.


00:22:02.624 --> 00:22:05.360
Thanks. l think you knocked out a filling.


00:22:05.458 --> 00:22:08.160
Well, l know the name of a good dentist
in town, if you need one.


00:22:08.257 --> 00:22:11.593
Thanks for the tip.
Maybe we can call it with your space phone.


00:22:12.991 --> 00:22:16.728
Space phone? Yeah, good one.
No, it's a radar antenna. Are you okay?


00:22:17.524 --> 00:22:18.758
Yeah, l'll let you know.


00:22:19.424 --> 00:22:22.960
l'm a zoologist.
l'm doing a project for the EPA on elk, so.


00:22:23.357 --> 00:22:26.927
Elk? Like deer with big antlers?


00:22:27.491 --> 00:22:29.526
Yeah, but don't tell the deer that.


00:22:38.624 --> 00:22:41.493
-Seriously, Connor? Stealing meat?
-No, l...


00:22:44.291 --> 00:22:49.162
Mr. Dimitri, l am so sorry.
He's never done anything like this before.


00:22:49.591 --> 00:22:50.758
Really?


00:22:52.591 --> 00:22:57.062
Yeah, he just loves meat.
Ever since he was wee high...


00:22:57.458 --> 00:22:58.559
Well, goody-goody for him.


00:22:59.391 --> 00:23:02.026
All he has to do now is pay for it.


00:23:02.124 --> 00:23:03.925
Nobody wants to buy used meat.


00:23:04.257 --> 00:23:05.291
No, of course.


00:23:05.558 --> 00:23:06.859
-lt's not for me, it's for...
-Connor,


00:23:07.724 --> 00:23:09.559
l want you to go straight home
and wait for me in your room.


00:23:10.791 --> 00:23:12.192
-But, Mom...
-Now.


00:23:17.257 --> 00:23:21.394
Look, l promise this will never happen again.


00:23:22.524 --> 00:23:24.158
He's a good kid, really. He's just...


00:23:25.691 --> 00:23:26.758
He's a little bored,


00:23:27.558 --> 00:23:29.493
and that is my fault, not his.


00:23:30.891 --> 00:23:33.693
So, how much do l owe you?


00:23:34.658 --> 00:23:38.261
Just to let you know,
the chicken went off sale yesterday.


00:23:38.891 --> 00:23:41.793
So, are they usually like that?


00:23:42.624 --> 00:23:45.626
Well, unless there's a species
of flying-elk-head l haven't heard of,


00:23:45.724 --> 00:23:47.559
l'm gonna go out on a limb and say no.


00:23:50.092 --> 00:23:51.693
Sorry. Excuse me.


00:23:55.825 --> 00:23:56.959
-Hello.
-Hey.


00:23:57.791 --> 00:23:59.893
l just got pulled away
from one of the biggest commissions


00:24:00.224 --> 00:24:03.827
of my life to bail your son from Dimitri's,


00:24:03.925 --> 00:24:06.527
where he was being held for shoplifting.


00:24:07.357 --> 00:24:13.596
Shoplifting? Okay, tell Dimitri
we'll pay for whatever candy bar he stole.


00:24:13.691 --> 00:24:17.227
l paid for it, honey, but it wasn't candy.


00:24:18.324 --> 00:24:20.592
No, he had a backpack full of meat.


00:24:21.257 --> 00:24:22.324
He's stealing meat?


00:24:22.624 --> 00:24:27.362
Yeah. And apparently,
he's taken up smoking.


00:24:28.025 --> 00:24:29.059
Smoking?


00:24:30.291 --> 00:24:33.027
So, remind me to put a lock
on the wine cabinet.


00:24:33.758 --> 00:24:36.393
He said they're Vica's
but she doesn't even smoke.


00:24:37.092 --> 00:24:38.359
And speaking of Vica,


00:24:38.458 --> 00:24:40.793
why are we paying her to sit at home
and watch TV


00:24:40.891 --> 00:24:42.792
whilst Connor is out shoplifting?


00:24:42.891 --> 00:24:45.126
Well, at least we're keeping one of them
off the street.


00:24:46.124 --> 00:24:49.560
Did we not feed Connor the right things
as a baby?


00:24:49.658 --> 00:24:52.427
Did l eat too much chili
when he was in my womb,


00:24:52.524 --> 00:24:54.392
and now he's a sociopath?


00:24:54.491 --> 00:24:56.492
What? He's not a sociopath.


00:24:56.591 --> 00:24:58.225
l mean, every kid does something like this
at some point.


00:24:58.324 --> 00:24:59.825
He's just... He's being a little boy.


00:24:59.925 --> 00:25:02.060
A little boy who's been unsupervised.


00:25:02.524 --> 00:25:04.392
Okay, put him on the phone,
l wanna talk to him.


00:25:05.858 --> 00:25:06.892
l sent him home.


00:25:07.658 --> 00:25:11.661
Sorry about your day. For what it's worth,
mine isn't going much better.


00:25:11.791 --> 00:25:17.029
Really? Sorry.
Okay, well, l'll see you at home.


00:25:17.124 --> 00:25:18.625
Okay. Bye, babe.


00:25:18.724 --> 00:25:22.961
Yeah. And l just hope you don't become
a vegetarian any time soon.


00:25:23.257 --> 00:25:24.691
l'm voting for pork chops.


00:25:25.391 --> 00:25:26.425
Bye.


00:25:31.991 --> 00:25:35.561
Sorry about that. Cell reception out here
is a once in a lifetime opportunity, so...


00:25:35.658 --> 00:25:38.260
Hey, what could have eaten the body?
A bear?


00:25:38.558 --> 00:25:40.860
l told you, l saw cougar tracks over there.


00:25:41.058 --> 00:25:43.493
He wasn't asking you, Charlie.
He was asking the zookeeper.


00:25:43.591 --> 00:25:44.625
Zoologist.


00:25:44.925 --> 00:25:47.027
-lsn't that what l said?
-No.


00:25:47.791 --> 00:25:51.227
l don't think it was a bear
but it may have been a coug'ar.


00:25:51.925 --> 00:25:53.126
What did l say?


00:25:53.424 --> 00:25:55.058
A cougar named Reba.


00:25:58.524 --> 00:26:00.759
-You know what you did?
-Yeah.


00:26:11.092 --> 00:26:13.427
Excuse me, sugar, could you pick that up?


00:26:18.291 --> 00:26:20.326
Thank you, handsome. You can keep it.


00:26:26.124 --> 00:26:28.893
Why would a hunter chop off the head?


00:26:28.991 --> 00:26:30.859
Yeah, isn't the head
supposed to be the best part?


00:26:31.391 --> 00:26:36.129
Well, that's what l keep trying to tell you,
but you don't wanna go for it.


00:26:38.558 --> 00:26:41.394
Well, it doesn't make rational sense, no.
But that might be the point.


00:26:41.491 --> 00:26:42.558
She might be trying to mess with me.


00:26:43.624 --> 00:26:44.725
Hunters are weird.


00:26:45.391 --> 00:26:46.458
Yes.


00:26:46.691 --> 00:26:50.061
So if it wasn't this cougar lady,
then what was it?


00:26:50.624 --> 00:26:52.058
l don't know.


00:26:53.025 --> 00:26:54.526
Look, if you guys run into any trouble,


00:26:54.624 --> 00:26:56.659
there's a cabin
just on the other side of that point.


00:26:56.758 --> 00:26:59.460
You can duck in there if you'd like, okay?


00:26:59.558 --> 00:27:01.226
Yeah, what kind of trouble?


00:27:01.558 --> 00:27:04.560
Just be safe and don't mess with the elk.


00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:07.892
All right? Sorry.


00:27:09.092 --> 00:27:11.794
-l hope you find your moose killer.
-Elk!


00:27:12.324 --> 00:27:13.391
Whatever.


00:27:13.691 --> 00:27:16.760
Excuse me,
is there a Reba around here anywhere?


00:27:17.558 --> 00:27:19.259
Just there? Thanks.


00:27:21.291 --> 00:27:22.325
Excuse me.


00:27:22.724 --> 00:27:25.093
-You Reba?
-Depends on who's asking.


00:27:25.624 --> 00:27:26.858
l contacted you, l'm Brett.


00:27:28.424 --> 00:27:30.192
Then that would make me Reba. Have a seat.


00:27:37.391 --> 00:27:42.829
Now, if l may say so, that photo in your ad,
it just don't do you no justice, Reba.


00:27:43.958 --> 00:27:45.826
Now, my good buddy Walt here and myself,


00:27:46.825 --> 00:27:50.195
we thought we were just getting ourselves
a hunting guide,


00:27:50.291 --> 00:27:54.261
but, girl, you are one fine package.


00:27:55.691 --> 00:27:59.227
Well, aren't you just such a sweet talker.


00:28:03.025 --> 00:28:07.662
Once we're miles away from civilization,
been out there a few days,


00:28:07.758 --> 00:28:11.495
missed everything you shot at,
and your belly starts grumbling,


00:28:11.591 --> 00:28:16.796
you're gonna appreciate my aim
a lot more than my other assets.


00:28:17.124 --> 00:28:18.391
lf you receive my meaning.


00:28:19.791 --> 00:28:23.995
Well, l, for one, am a multi-tasker
and l plan on appreciating both.


00:28:28.025 --> 00:28:29.059
So,


00:28:30.624 --> 00:28:33.660
Brett, was it? How'd you hear about Reba?


00:28:35.224 --> 00:28:36.258
lnternet.


00:28:37.291 --> 00:28:38.525
lnternet.


00:28:41.424 --> 00:28:43.692
How about you two load your gear
into my truck?


00:28:43.791 --> 00:28:45.893
lt's the big one out front.


00:28:45.991 --> 00:28:48.493
Boat on the back, gun rack up front,


00:28:49.224 --> 00:28:53.261
mildly offensive bumper-sticker. You'll see.


00:28:53.458 --> 00:28:55.760
All right. Let's go, Walt.


00:28:55.925 --> 00:28:56.925
Hey, hey, hey, hey.


00:28:59.558 --> 00:29:01.426
All right. There.


00:29:03.724 --> 00:29:04.858
Thank you.


00:29:09.025 --> 00:29:10.393
So, Brett?


00:29:12.324 --> 00:29:14.793
You play your cards pretty close to the vest,


00:29:17.025 --> 00:29:19.460
but l think l deserve to know
what you're really doing here.


00:29:20.724 --> 00:29:21.724
Your website said that...


00:29:22.257 --> 00:29:24.092
l don't have a website.


00:29:29.591 --> 00:29:32.694
Well, let's just say you're kind of a legend.


00:29:34.558 --> 00:29:35.792
A legend?


00:29:36.691 --> 00:29:38.125
Of what sort?


00:29:38.224 --> 00:29:40.726
Bigfoot? Crop circles?


00:29:41.458 --> 00:29:42.492
Global warming?


00:29:42.591 --> 00:29:46.394
No. You know how to find things
that don't wanna be found.


00:29:48.524 --> 00:29:50.058
l'm looking for a girl.


00:29:51.257 --> 00:29:53.492
A girl that hangs out in the woods?


00:29:54.191 --> 00:29:56.426
Or the lake. l'm not really sure.


00:29:59.324 --> 00:30:01.893
All right, look. l don't have a chance
of finding her on my own,


00:30:01.991 --> 00:30:03.959
and you're the only guide
that goes into the area.


00:30:07.424 --> 00:30:08.925
All right, then.


00:30:10.124 --> 00:30:15.262
Elks for the yahoos.
One Lois Lane for Superman here.


00:30:32.324 --> 00:30:33.324
Where is it?


00:30:43.391 --> 00:30:44.558
The meat stealer.


00:30:45.591 --> 00:30:47.326
Your mother called. Go to room.


00:30:47.491 --> 00:30:49.826
-Lost something? Like a lighter?
-Give it back.


00:30:51.724 --> 00:30:53.025
You tried to get me in trouble


00:30:53.124 --> 00:30:55.192
by putting this and the cigarettes
in my backpack.


00:30:55.558 --> 00:30:56.825
Give it back right now.


00:30:57.458 --> 00:30:59.626
And you can ask my mom
for the cigarettes.


00:31:05.257 --> 00:31:07.292
Teddy? Teddy?


00:31:29.324 --> 00:31:33.528
Connor! Come back here.
Your mother will be mad at me.


00:31:54.257 --> 00:31:56.459
Devil child, where did you go?


00:32:29.424 --> 00:32:33.494
Okay, so l'm down to one hotdog.
You guys are gonna have to share.


00:32:38.391 --> 00:32:39.558
Connor!


00:32:44.157 --> 00:32:45.525
lt was here.


00:32:50.691 --> 00:32:54.461
Nathan, l am sick and tired
of these false alarms and pranks.


00:32:55.624 --> 00:32:58.259
Now, l drove all the way out here
because you promised me a bloody mess.


00:32:58.357 --> 00:33:01.560
-Now, where is it?
-lt was right here.


00:33:06.291 --> 00:33:07.925
Teddy, stay.


00:33:08.357 --> 00:33:09.958
Come on, Teddy, get away from there.


00:33:16.391 --> 00:33:17.391
Wait.


00:33:22.092 --> 00:33:23.393
Teddy, no.


00:33:24.092 --> 00:33:25.092
Watch yourself.


00:33:27.724 --> 00:33:29.992
Teddy, no! Come back, Teddy. No.


00:33:44.858 --> 00:33:45.959
lt's a stick.


00:33:46.324 --> 00:33:47.391
Yeah.


00:33:48.925 --> 00:33:51.627
Poor Teddy,
now l know why you have a panic attack.


00:34:03.958 --> 00:34:06.293
-How many elk did you say you've lost?
-ln the last six months?


00:34:06.491 --> 00:34:07.491
Yeah.


00:34:08.058 --> 00:34:10.393
Too many.
l'm starting to think it's not a poacher.


00:34:11.357 --> 00:34:15.227
Hey, l checked that lake three times.


00:34:15.591 --> 00:34:19.127
And, Nathan, l swear to God
my eyes were open the whole time.


00:34:19.224 --> 00:34:21.859
Now look, l may be from the city,
but l know my way around the wilderness.


00:34:22.324 --> 00:34:26.061
Last time you checked that lake was a year
and a half ago, and things change.


00:34:26.157 --> 00:34:28.759
Now, we owe it to the community
to make sure that lake is clear.


00:34:28.858 --> 00:34:31.694
l don't live with my head in the sand.
l need evidence.


00:34:32.291 --> 00:34:33.458
Well, what if something just came
and ate it?


00:34:34.025 --> 00:34:36.794
And what if the evidence is a stick?


00:34:37.825 --> 00:34:40.561
l don't have sophisticated sonar equipment.


00:34:40.691 --> 00:34:43.260
We'd have to order it in.
That would take days.


00:34:45.124 --> 00:34:46.158
Okay.


00:34:47.791 --> 00:34:50.760
But we do have the next best thing
back at the station.


00:34:52.191 --> 00:34:53.559
Well, great.


00:34:54.357 --> 00:34:56.692
So you and l, we'll go back,
we'll come here, we'll check the lake.


00:34:56.791 --> 00:34:59.293
Now, nothing would make me happier
than for you to be right.


00:34:59.958 --> 00:35:02.627
All right. All right, let's go fishing.


00:35:27.958 --> 00:35:29.259
Yes, dear.


00:35:29.958 --> 00:35:32.460
Yes, dear. Why don't you do that?


00:35:35.424 --> 00:35:37.726
l bought this with my own money.


00:35:38.391 --> 00:35:41.660
You know, in New York City we got people
who swear they've seen Elvis


00:35:41.758 --> 00:35:43.659
at 63rd and Park.


00:35:43.758 --> 00:35:46.427
We got people
who swear they've been abducted by aliens


00:35:46.524 --> 00:35:50.594
and, yes, we've even got people
who swear they've seen albino crocodiles


00:35:50.958 --> 00:35:52.259
-in the subway.
-Sheriff!


00:35:52.357 --> 00:35:53.424
Shut up!


00:36:05.558 --> 00:36:09.628
Wow! That's a little much
for Aroostook County, don't you think?


00:36:10.191 --> 00:36:15.195
l believe a boy scout
should always be prepared.


00:36:16.624 --> 00:36:18.292
Especially one from Jersey.


00:36:18.391 --> 00:36:19.558
Connor?


00:36:26.458 --> 00:36:27.525
Vica?


00:36:30.925 --> 00:36:32.092
Connor!


00:36:50.691 --> 00:36:54.428
l think the sun is better over here.


00:37:27.925 --> 00:37:30.994
Connor? Connor, are you here?


00:37:32.825 --> 00:37:35.527
You know, l told you to go straight home.


00:37:36.058 --> 00:37:37.225
Connor!


00:37:39.157 --> 00:37:40.157
Mom,


00:37:41.257 --> 00:37:42.591
l think l did something bad.


00:37:42.691 --> 00:37:45.060
-Sweetie, is that blood?
-No, no, no.


00:37:45.157 --> 00:37:47.359
-What is...
-lt's not my blood. It's...


00:37:48.291 --> 00:37:49.425
l was by the lake...


00:38:01.758 --> 00:38:04.460
ln the water. He's in the water!


00:38:20.191 --> 00:38:21.191
You coming, Ellie?


00:38:21.858 --> 00:38:22.892
lsn't it a little cold?


00:38:24.092 --> 00:38:25.426
That's why we came out here.


00:38:25.658 --> 00:38:28.594
Get out into the real world,
the way things used to be.


00:38:29.257 --> 00:38:32.126
You know, when our ancestors came here,
there were no heated pools.


00:38:32.691 --> 00:38:35.393
There didn't have iPods either,
but l noticed you brought yours.


00:38:35.791 --> 00:38:38.093
Hey, at least you got away
from he-who-must-not-be-named.


00:38:38.191 --> 00:38:39.825
Yeah, let's not talk about it, okay?


00:38:40.224 --> 00:38:42.926
l bought a new bikini for this trip,
so l have to use it,


00:38:43.025 --> 00:38:44.793
whether the water is freezing or not.


00:38:45.791 --> 00:38:46.858
See, now she's got the right idea.


00:38:48.491 --> 00:38:50.659
Or, l have a better idea.


00:38:51.224 --> 00:38:53.292
Why don't we all just jump in naked?


00:38:53.391 --> 00:38:55.459
That'd be hilarious, right?


00:38:56.624 --> 00:38:57.958
You guys first.


00:39:02.092 --> 00:39:03.059
lt worked!


00:39:03.825 --> 00:39:06.394
Yeah, l guess the image of you naked
really did the trick.


00:39:19.257 --> 00:39:21.225
He actually thought
we were gonna jump in there naked.


00:39:21.324 --> 00:39:22.625
l know. He is so...


00:39:22.724 --> 00:39:24.725
-Obnoxious, right?
-l was gonna say funny.


00:39:25.558 --> 00:39:26.592
You're kidding.


00:39:26.691 --> 00:39:28.893
Not like ''l'm gonna sleep with him'' funny,


00:39:28.991 --> 00:39:31.593
but like, ''l'd set him up
with one of my fat friends'' funny.


00:39:31.724 --> 00:39:34.026
Like you have any fat friends.


00:39:34.124 --> 00:39:36.626
-Clarissa put on a ton of weight recently.
-Tara!


00:39:36.991 --> 00:39:40.027
-What?
-She's pregnant, not fat.


00:39:40.458 --> 00:39:44.461
lt's not all baby. She's not giving birth
to, like, Andre the freaking Giant.


00:39:44.624 --> 00:39:45.891
You're terrible.


00:39:46.558 --> 00:39:48.660
Just being realistic.


00:39:51.324 --> 00:39:52.658
That's a really cute bikini.


00:39:52.758 --> 00:39:54.059
-Where'd you get that?
-Thanks. Clarissa's closet.


00:39:54.391 --> 00:39:55.692
Have you heard from Brett?


00:39:55.791 --> 00:39:57.826
,
No, if l wanted to talk to Brett
l would have called him, so...


00:39:58.257 --> 00:39:59.958
Well, you're not gonna let him apologize?


00:40:00.058 --> 00:40:02.927
l'm gonna let him stew for a few days,
or weeks. l haven't decided.


00:40:03.391 --> 00:40:04.425
Would you?


00:40:04.858 --> 00:40:06.059
Does he know about you and Aaron?


00:40:06.257 --> 00:40:07.291
What?


00:40:07.391 --> 00:40:09.493
No, there's nothing to know.


00:40:09.591 --> 00:40:13.027
Yeah, and l'm not gonna hook up
with the lacrosse team.


00:40:13.458 --> 00:40:15.293
-Seriously, there's nothing.
-Yeah, right.


00:40:15.658 --> 00:40:16.692
Honest.


00:40:17.691 --> 00:40:18.725
You ready?


00:40:18.825 --> 00:40:21.327
-Yeah, let's go.
-lt's gonna be cold.


00:40:35.524 --> 00:40:36.958
Oh, God.


00:40:43.658 --> 00:40:44.992
Oh, my God!


00:40:57.424 --> 00:40:59.192
lt's good though, eh?


00:41:11.624 --> 00:41:14.927
-What's going on?
-l can't get through to my wife.


00:41:15.157 --> 00:41:18.260
l haven't been able to get through to mine
since '86.


00:41:21.424 --> 00:41:23.225
Connor, try 911 again.


00:41:26.591 --> 00:41:27.858
lt won't go through.


00:41:28.891 --> 00:41:30.192
Vica? Vica? Hold still, honey.


00:41:30.391 --> 00:41:32.126
This is gonna hurt even worse.


00:41:34.092 --> 00:41:37.462
Connor, find me something
to soak up the blood. Now, now, now.


00:41:38.025 --> 00:41:40.093
Well, Susan isn't gonna believe this.


00:41:41.424 --> 00:41:43.692
l mean, ''What did you do today?''


00:41:45.658 --> 00:41:47.226
''l hunted a crocodile.''


00:41:48.958 --> 00:41:50.159
You're all worked up over this, aren't you?


00:41:50.691 --> 00:41:51.725
Yeah.


00:41:54.157 --> 00:41:56.125
Okay. Here.


00:41:59.724 --> 00:42:00.791
l'm sorry.


00:42:01.925 --> 00:42:05.995
Okay. Connor, start talking.


00:42:06.691 --> 00:42:08.192
l just wanted a pet.


00:42:08.424 --> 00:42:09.625
Sweetie, what was it?


00:42:15.991 --> 00:42:17.058
Mom!


00:42:23.825 --> 00:42:24.825
Hey, Suze, guess what?


00:42:25.124 --> 00:42:26.191
Vica...


00:42:26.291 --> 00:42:27.892
-You there?
-We don't know what...


00:42:28.558 --> 00:42:29.725
-Can you hear me?
-Okay, Susan,


00:42:30.191 --> 00:42:31.759
try to speak a little more slowly


00:42:31.858 --> 00:42:33.226
-and calm down.
-...at the cabin.


00:42:33.458 --> 00:42:35.126
She's at the cabin. She's terrified.


00:42:35.224 --> 00:42:38.193
-And... And l don't know what...
-Okay. Hey...


00:42:40.558 --> 00:42:42.159
Come on. Let's load the guns.


00:42:51.058 --> 00:42:53.660
lt's not that l didn't wanna let
the poor bastard live,


00:42:53.758 --> 00:42:57.528
it's just, how many times do you get
to shoot a giraffe?


00:42:59.025 --> 00:43:00.793
-Hey.
-Anyway, the zoo


00:43:01.291 --> 00:43:05.428
demoted me to the souvenir shop after that.
Can you imagine?


00:43:06.624 --> 00:43:07.925
You're joking, right?


00:43:08.591 --> 00:43:10.359
You shot an animal in captivity?


00:43:10.458 --> 00:43:13.260
Just further proving
that my philosophy is correct.


00:43:13.991 --> 00:43:18.261
Hunting's not fair,
so there's no point in pretending otherwise.


00:43:21.925 --> 00:43:23.359
What's that?


00:43:23.458 --> 00:43:28.362
This is what guarantees you a shot
at the big game.


00:43:30.324 --> 00:43:33.026
Big game is what you're after. Right, Brett?


00:43:35.157 --> 00:43:37.993
Nothing like shooting and eating an animal
you're not supposed to.


00:43:40.524 --> 00:43:42.025
Stop the boat.


00:43:42.391 --> 00:43:45.127
l usually don't take orders,
but l'll let that one slide.


00:43:46.058 --> 00:43:47.659
What'd you see, college boy, a turtle?


00:43:47.891 --> 00:43:48.925
Quiet.


00:43:49.058 --> 00:43:54.029
Okay, that one l'm not gonna let slide.
That's gonna cost you an extra 20.


00:44:07.524 --> 00:44:09.859
What did you see?
Did you see Vica get bitten?


00:44:09.958 --> 00:44:11.359
-No.
-Then whose blood is this?


00:44:12.825 --> 00:44:13.892
Teddy's.


00:44:14.724 --> 00:44:15.791
He went too close to the water


00:44:15.891 --> 00:44:19.160
and l tried calling him
and he wouldn't listen.


00:44:22.958 --> 00:44:23.992
Mom?


00:44:24.791 --> 00:44:25.858
Yeah?


00:44:26.524 --> 00:44:27.691
l fed them.


00:44:28.958 --> 00:44:29.958
What?


00:44:31.925 --> 00:44:33.559
The meat from our freezer.


00:44:33.658 --> 00:44:37.028
And that's why l stole from the store,
because l couldn't feed them enough.


00:44:38.025 --> 00:44:40.293
That's why they ate Vica's dog.


00:44:40.524 --> 00:44:41.558
Connor,


00:44:43.424 --> 00:44:45.292
you've been coming here,
when we told you not to?


00:44:45.825 --> 00:44:46.926
On my bike.


00:44:47.658 --> 00:44:49.326
You knew there were dangerous animals
in the lake


00:44:49.424 --> 00:44:51.759
-and you didn't tell us?
-You would have made Dad kill them.


00:44:53.025 --> 00:44:56.528
Oh, my God. No, no, sweetie, he would...
He would never have done that.


00:44:56.624 --> 00:44:58.125
He would have moved them


00:44:58.224 --> 00:45:00.492
and taken them someplace safe.


00:45:04.058 --> 00:45:05.058
ls she going to be okay?


00:45:07.324 --> 00:45:09.626
l don't know, sweetie. l...


00:45:10.991 --> 00:45:13.393
Try the phone again, please.


00:45:17.958 --> 00:45:21.461
Okay. Okay, Connor,


00:45:23.524 --> 00:45:24.992
we have to get Vica into the car


00:45:25.825 --> 00:45:27.760
and get her to the hospital. Okay?


00:45:28.624 --> 00:45:30.525
Yeah, but what if they come back?


00:45:45.025 --> 00:45:48.094
Doesn't all this take
some of the fun out of it?


00:45:51.391 --> 00:45:53.559
You know what? You're right.


00:45:54.458 --> 00:45:55.892
l think that actually,


00:45:55.991 --> 00:45:59.694
we should track their footprints
and sniff the ground


00:45:59.791 --> 00:46:02.393
to see where they mark their territory.


00:46:04.891 --> 00:46:06.659
All right, guys, close enough.


00:46:06.758 --> 00:46:09.360
We'll let your predator instincts
take over from here, okay?


00:46:09.458 --> 00:46:10.759
-Yep.
-All right.


00:46:12.524 --> 00:46:14.859
This is the fun part.


00:46:33.591 --> 00:46:36.327
Walt! Walt! Walt!


00:47:00.424 --> 00:47:03.593
No. No. Get off of me.


00:47:06.257 --> 00:47:08.192
-Hurry up.
-There's a crocodile.


00:47:08.291 --> 00:47:10.126
-Walt!
-Come on, get her here.


00:47:15.191 --> 00:47:18.694
No. Get off of me. Get off of me. Walt!


00:47:18.791 --> 00:47:20.259
No, don't be an idiot.


00:47:21.324 --> 00:47:22.558
Now get off!


00:47:25.658 --> 00:47:30.596
Damn it. That ain't right.
That ain't anything close to right.


00:47:30.691 --> 00:47:32.359
We need to get the hell out of here.


00:47:32.458 --> 00:47:34.726
Yeah? To where?


00:47:34.825 --> 00:47:36.193
Hey, you're the guide, you tell me.


00:47:44.291 --> 00:47:46.960
-No. No. We can't just leave Walt.
-Of course we can.


00:47:48.025 --> 00:47:50.026
Something just ripped him
to pieces back there.


00:47:50.124 --> 00:47:53.760
But l know, let's all get back in the water.
You grab an arm, you grab a leg


00:47:53.858 --> 00:47:56.293
-and l'll just bring up the rear.
-Shut up.


00:47:56.991 --> 00:47:57.958
Shut up?


00:47:59.558 --> 00:48:01.760
-Shut up? Shut up?
-Just calm down. Relax.


00:48:01.858 --> 00:48:03.025
-Come on.
-You shut up!


00:48:03.124 --> 00:48:04.325
Hey!


00:48:11.424 --> 00:48:12.424
Charlie?


00:48:12.825 --> 00:48:17.196
Hey, man, Tara needs you.
Somebody needs to check her for ticks.


00:48:23.858 --> 00:48:26.327
Okay, Charlie. Enough's enough.


00:48:26.791 --> 00:48:29.193
This isn't funny anymore.
Get your ass back here.


00:48:29.291 --> 00:48:31.660
God. Which direction did he go?


00:48:32.591 --> 00:48:35.961
Knowing Charlie, he's probably finding
a quiet spot to whack off.


00:48:36.624 --> 00:48:39.259
Why did we have to bring him?
He gives me the creeps.


00:48:39.391 --> 00:48:41.493
We shouldn't have brought either of them.


00:48:41.591 --> 00:48:45.294
lt would have given us a chance to be alone
and get to know each other better.


00:48:46.291 --> 00:48:48.559
So, that's what this is about, huh?


00:48:48.958 --> 00:48:50.559
l thought it was pretty obvious.


00:48:52.691 --> 00:48:54.859
You know, the first time l met you,


00:48:56.191 --> 00:48:58.893
well, you had me after hello.


00:49:00.858 --> 00:49:04.094
Look, let's find Charlie first, okay?


00:49:04.524 --> 00:49:07.159
Then we can talk
about what other movie lines you know.


00:49:09.092 --> 00:49:13.362
First you said you didn't like it out here,
and then it was too cold,


00:49:13.458 --> 00:49:16.160
now you wanna waste your time
Iooking for Charlie goofball.


00:49:16.257 --> 00:49:19.026
You certainly bitch and moan a lot.
You know, l thought you'd be grateful


00:49:19.124 --> 00:49:21.025
l asked you along,
considering the alternative.


00:49:31.224 --> 00:49:33.125
You guys?


00:49:33.458 --> 00:49:36.060
Charlie, is that you?


00:49:46.157 --> 00:49:48.125
Mail order piece of crap.


00:49:49.491 --> 00:49:50.758
lt doesn't work.


00:49:56.624 --> 00:49:59.026
Here, this is for you.


00:50:03.092 --> 00:50:05.194
This has got explosive shells in it.


00:50:07.124 --> 00:50:10.360
And this, this is a shark stick.


00:50:11.025 --> 00:50:13.927
Works like a shotgun, but under water.


00:50:14.058 --> 00:50:16.927
One shot from this
will take the head right off a great white.


00:50:17.591 --> 00:50:20.427
You're not a tranquilizer dart
sort of guy, are you?


00:50:21.825 --> 00:50:23.493
Damn straight.


00:50:23.591 --> 00:50:28.996
lf we run into this mythical ''crocodile''
of yours, let's get one thing straight.


00:50:29.092 --> 00:50:32.595
l don't want any of your EPA,
endangered species crap.


00:50:32.691 --> 00:50:34.426
-Are we on the same page?
-Yeah.


00:50:36.624 --> 00:50:39.727
God, Charlie. If you wanna be
a Peeping Tom, l'll save you the trouble.


00:50:41.658 --> 00:50:46.829
What the... Ellie, Aaron!
There's another one of those deer things.


00:50:58.491 --> 00:50:59.692
What's that?


00:51:01.724 --> 00:51:02.958
Where'd it come from?


00:51:05.591 --> 00:51:07.125
l'm not even sure l heard it.


00:51:10.291 --> 00:51:11.592
Ellie.


00:51:16.124 --> 00:51:18.125
So, what do you think did this?


00:51:18.925 --> 00:51:20.192
l bet it was a shark.


00:51:22.958 --> 00:51:24.292
A big shark, a Megalodon.


00:51:25.191 --> 00:51:28.227
A megalo-what?
What the hell have you been smoking?


00:51:28.858 --> 00:51:30.826
That's Charlie Burman,
he's a college student.


00:51:30.925 --> 00:51:35.329
He's here on a backpacking trip.
He's friends with this guy l know.


00:51:36.558 --> 00:51:39.360
l came out here to find my girlfriend
to stop her from doing something stupid.


00:51:41.191 --> 00:51:44.761
Yeah, well, it seems like coming out here
was already pretty stupid.


00:51:47.891 --> 00:51:49.692
Sorry about your friend.


00:51:50.257 --> 00:51:54.527
l hated him. He's an idiot and a pervert.


00:51:55.825 --> 00:51:59.295
Yeah? Then l'm sorry he smells so bad.


00:52:15.058 --> 00:52:16.325
So, what do we do now?


00:52:16.925 --> 00:52:19.093
ln your case, l'd finish high school.


00:52:19.191 --> 00:52:21.893
Until then, get back to the lake
and find our guns.


00:52:23.524 --> 00:52:24.758
They're back.


00:52:25.257 --> 00:52:28.994
Connor, come away from the window.
They can smell you through the glass.


00:52:29.092 --> 00:52:31.727
-ls that true?
-l don't know, honey. Just...


00:52:43.825 --> 00:52:45.026
-Connor.
-Dad!


00:52:48.758 --> 00:52:49.892
Nathan!


00:52:50.291 --> 00:52:52.693
Susan, stay away from the window!


00:52:54.157 --> 00:52:56.058
The bathroom.
There's thick walls in the bathroom.


00:52:56.157 --> 00:52:57.358
Help me with Vica.


00:53:01.891 --> 00:53:03.692
Let them get closer.


00:53:05.758 --> 00:53:07.759
Lay down. Here you go.


00:53:10.491 --> 00:53:11.491
Five,


00:53:13.925 --> 00:53:17.094
four, three...


00:53:17.191 --> 00:53:18.825
Down, honey. Down.


00:53:19.691 --> 00:53:22.393
...two, one.


00:53:45.558 --> 00:53:47.760
Honey, it's fine. Stay here, okay?


00:53:47.858 --> 00:53:49.159
-But, Mom...
-Connor!


00:54:14.224 --> 00:54:15.858
Oh, my God.


00:54:45.925 --> 00:54:48.794
-Nathan!
-Hey, you okay?


00:54:50.458 --> 00:54:52.726
-Where's Connor?
-Dad!


00:54:52.825 --> 00:54:55.160
-Connor! Hey, you okay?
-Yeah.


00:55:32.858 --> 00:55:34.960
-Tony?
-Open up.


00:55:42.591 --> 00:55:44.960
l officially owe you an apology.


00:55:48.291 --> 00:55:51.694
Great. Now she's gone.
Where the hell is she?


00:55:52.092 --> 00:55:53.359
Tara!


00:55:54.858 --> 00:55:58.228
No. No. No! No!


00:55:59.825 --> 00:56:02.060
She was... She was...


00:56:03.324 --> 00:56:07.428
lt's okay. It's okay. Come on. Come on.
It's okay. It's okay.


00:56:07.524 --> 00:56:10.760
Don't worry. Don't worry.
It's going to be okay.


00:56:20.858 --> 00:56:22.459
Could be a gator.


00:56:26.524 --> 00:56:31.061
l'm sure she's fine,
this damsel in distress of yours.


00:56:32.424 --> 00:56:36.995
This is about another guy. Yeah.
She goes on a camping trip without you,


00:56:37.092 --> 00:56:42.163
so you hire a hunting guide
to help you stalk her through a state forest.


00:56:42.257 --> 00:56:43.458
Totally normal.


00:56:46.257 --> 00:56:48.425
For a complete jealous psycho.


00:56:49.524 --> 00:56:51.392
What she do,
forget her chastity belt at home?


00:56:52.424 --> 00:56:56.027
lt's a little more complicated than that,
and it's not your damn problem.


00:56:56.925 --> 00:56:58.192
Not my problem?


00:56:58.291 --> 00:57:02.695
Hey, getting you all back in one piece
is my responsibility,


00:57:02.858 --> 00:57:05.694
and l take it very seriously,
thank you very much.


00:57:06.257 --> 00:57:08.359
So the least you could do


00:57:08.458 --> 00:57:12.762
is drop your ''l got a stick
up my college educated butt'' attitude.


00:57:15.825 --> 00:57:18.928
Yes, she came with another guy.


00:57:23.092 --> 00:57:24.526
Damn, l'm good.


00:57:28.025 --> 00:57:31.862
Hey, now guess what l found.


00:57:36.391 --> 00:57:41.429
Now, before we all got unceremoniously
jacked from my boat,


00:57:41.624 --> 00:57:44.393
we were following a tracking signal
from an elk.


00:57:44.491 --> 00:57:46.326
Now that elk, it seems, is actually


00:57:46.424 --> 00:57:49.927
passing through the digestive tract
of our gator friend.


00:57:53.524 --> 00:57:56.827
l'm sorry to put it this way,
but predators go to where their food is.


00:57:56.925 --> 00:58:00.895
So whatever killed smelly over there
knows where your girlfriend is.


00:58:00.991 --> 00:58:03.393
Now, all we have to do is follow him. Okay?


00:58:06.191 --> 00:58:09.160
Come on, baby. Come on, talk to Mama.


00:58:11.224 --> 00:58:12.491
Yes.


00:58:15.891 --> 00:58:18.960
We could go to that guy's cabin
across the lake, try to find some help.


00:58:19.058 --> 00:58:20.058
Relax.


00:58:20.157 --> 00:58:22.325
That guy who works for the state,
he'd know who to call.


00:58:22.424 --> 00:58:24.959
We don't need any help, l can handle this.


00:58:27.591 --> 00:58:30.694
lsn't this what you wanted?
A bit of time away from the world?


00:58:30.791 --> 00:58:35.829
l wanted to forget about Brett for a few days.
Not get lost in the Land of the Lost.


00:58:36.691 --> 00:58:39.994
Hell, at least if Brett was here,
he wouldn't give up on finding his friends.


00:58:40.092 --> 00:58:41.860
Well, you seem to have forgotten
about him all right.


00:58:43.257 --> 00:58:47.928
Look, l'm just trying to help. That's all.


00:58:51.791 --> 00:58:57.196
Seriously? My best friend is missing.
We need to get help.


00:59:20.124 --> 00:59:21.358
Nothing bigger than a trout?


00:59:26.357 --> 00:59:29.560
l'd say that thing's
a little bigger than a goddamn trout!


00:59:31.458 --> 00:59:36.062
l know this is just a job for you,
but everyone l have left is in this room,


00:59:36.157 --> 00:59:39.460
and they're in danger because l trusted you.


00:59:40.958 --> 00:59:42.526
lt's gotta be 25 feet long.


00:59:43.191 --> 00:59:46.460
l screwed up. Is that what you wanna hear?
l'm sorry.


00:59:46.558 --> 00:59:50.228
The big one, l have no idea.
It could have been dropped from the sky.


00:59:50.324 --> 00:59:51.758
Yeah, dropped from...


00:59:58.257 --> 00:59:59.324
The elk.


01:00:02.092 --> 01:00:05.662
Three years ago, the EPA re-introduced elk
just down the river.


01:00:06.092 --> 01:00:08.160
Predators move towards their food.


01:00:09.758 --> 01:00:14.696
lt is possible that it didn't show up
on your sonar because it wasn't in the lake.


01:00:15.324 --> 01:00:17.926
Question is, why'd they come back here?


01:00:18.025 --> 01:00:19.025
l don't...


01:00:19.124 --> 01:00:21.192
l mean, did the big one follow the elk
into the area?


01:00:21.291 --> 01:00:22.258
l don't know.


01:00:23.591 --> 01:00:27.661
lt's an answer for the big one,
but the smaller ones,


01:00:27.758 --> 01:00:31.294
they've been here for months.
Talk to your son.


01:00:39.157 --> 01:00:43.361
Hey, l'm gonna go check and see
what kind of shampoo you use.


01:00:50.058 --> 01:00:51.793
You knew about them?


01:01:01.591 --> 01:01:03.359
Come here. Come here.


01:01:05.092 --> 01:01:07.594
ls this where you've been going
on your bike every day?


01:01:08.458 --> 01:01:12.195
You know, they almost killed Vica?
You know they can kill you?


01:01:12.491 --> 01:01:17.229
-Never hurt me.
-Listen! They're not your friends.


01:01:17.791 --> 01:01:22.295
They're wild animals. And wild animals
live by a set of rules to ensure their survival.


01:01:22.391 --> 01:01:25.994
One of the rules is that they eat
anything smaller than they are.


01:01:27.357 --> 01:01:30.660
Do you understand that?
They're not your friends.


01:01:30.758 --> 01:01:34.862
lt was just something cool to play with.
Both of you left me alone.


01:01:35.291 --> 01:01:37.559
You care more about your stupid elk
than me,


01:01:37.658 --> 01:01:39.659
and Mom's always working.


01:01:40.524 --> 01:01:44.427
You know, l thought it was a rule of nature
that parents took care of their kids.


01:01:45.324 --> 01:01:46.758
My mistake.


01:02:06.958 --> 01:02:07.925
Hey.


01:02:12.724 --> 01:02:16.194
So, still think we can get a good price
for this place?


01:02:24.825 --> 01:02:30.230
lt's a fixer-upper, real curb-appeal,
pets included.


01:02:31.758 --> 01:02:36.996
Yeah. And l, for one, am ready
to say goodbye to lake-side living forever.


01:02:40.758 --> 01:02:43.293
Sweets, l think we should
make a break for it.


01:02:43.391 --> 01:02:45.392
l don't think Vica's gonna make it if we wait


01:02:45.491 --> 01:02:47.559
and we still have a couple hours
of daylight left.


01:02:47.658 --> 01:02:50.160
-Yeah, but she can't walk.
-We can carry her.


01:02:53.224 --> 01:02:54.458
l know you're scared.


01:02:55.524 --> 01:03:00.762
But with Willinger covering us,
we should be able to make it.


01:03:04.458 --> 01:03:05.525
Okay.


01:03:06.491 --> 01:03:07.458
You sure?


01:03:13.658 --> 01:03:16.861
We're gonna have to get the car close
if we're gonna get everyone inside.


01:03:16.958 --> 01:03:18.959
-All right.
-Okay.


01:03:20.025 --> 01:03:24.062
Connor, take care of your mother. Okay?


01:03:24.724 --> 01:03:26.358
-Okay.
-Okay.


01:03:31.124 --> 01:03:32.959
Looks like
we're actually gonna do this thing.


01:03:33.191 --> 01:03:34.225
l love you.


01:03:44.424 --> 01:03:45.691
-lf something happens...
-lt won't.


01:03:47.191 --> 01:03:50.227
But if it does, l'll keep Connor safe, okay?


01:03:50.858 --> 01:03:53.527
Well, l was gonna say, ''Come save us.''


01:04:10.157 --> 01:04:11.157
Let's do this.


01:04:25.591 --> 01:04:27.459
Come on, come on. Come on, come on.


01:04:27.558 --> 01:04:28.525
Go.


01:04:31.758 --> 01:04:33.292
-Let's go!
-l'm trying!


01:04:57.124 --> 01:04:58.291
That one's new!


01:05:00.357 --> 01:05:03.493
Mom, Mom, what are you doing?


01:05:03.591 --> 01:05:05.225
Connor, stay here. l mean it.


01:05:08.025 --> 01:05:10.894
-Mom, you have to press the red button.
-What?


01:05:15.224 --> 01:05:17.559
-How do you know that stuff?
-lt's always the red button.


01:05:18.458 --> 01:05:19.425
Mom!


01:05:23.124 --> 01:05:25.192
Susan, get back in the house.


01:05:30.357 --> 01:05:31.524
Susan!


01:05:39.724 --> 01:05:40.724
Mom!


01:05:47.257 --> 01:05:49.492
Hey! Get away from her.


01:05:52.491 --> 01:05:53.592
Come on.


01:05:59.491 --> 01:06:01.025
No, no, no, no, no.


01:06:21.257 --> 01:06:23.292
Susan, get to the cabin!


01:06:27.058 --> 01:06:28.092
Go now! Go!


01:06:38.624 --> 01:06:39.658
lt's locked!


01:06:43.424 --> 01:06:45.459
-Vica!
-Vica, open the door.


01:06:45.558 --> 01:06:47.326
-Vica!
-Vica!


01:06:48.424 --> 01:06:49.725
Open the door!


01:07:03.858 --> 01:07:06.293
Go, go. Back there.


01:07:06.391 --> 01:07:08.860
-l wanna help!
-Now, Connor!


01:07:11.791 --> 01:07:14.193
Vica! Vica!


01:07:15.791 --> 01:07:17.192
He's coming through.


01:07:39.092 --> 01:07:41.627
You got us turned around.
l don't even know which way camp was.


01:07:41.724 --> 01:07:43.859
l heard a noise towards this way.


01:07:43.958 --> 01:07:46.794
You heard gunshots.
Do we really wanna go towards gunshots?


01:07:46.891 --> 01:07:49.226
We wanna go towards...


01:07:53.925 --> 01:07:55.893
Oh, my God!


01:07:56.658 --> 01:08:00.094
Oh, my God. We need to get the hell
away from here. Now!


01:08:00.191 --> 01:08:01.926
-Tara!
-Who the hell cares about Tara?


01:08:02.025 --> 01:08:03.359
-Get up. Don't cry. Come on.
-l can't.


01:08:03.458 --> 01:08:05.426
-l can't.
-l'm not gonna say it again.


01:08:05.524 --> 01:08:08.760
Get up, damn it.
Stop being a little bitch and get up.


01:08:10.357 --> 01:08:12.659
Look, l'm going this way
with or without you.


01:08:14.191 --> 01:08:16.459
-Look, it's Brett's jacket. Brett's jacket.
-What, are you crazy?


01:08:16.558 --> 01:08:18.927
l don't know what the hell is going on here,
but we need to leave.


01:08:19.025 --> 01:08:20.292
l think he's looking for me.


01:08:22.058 --> 01:08:26.495
You can't be serious.
You think Brett gives a rat's ass about you?


01:08:26.591 --> 01:08:29.293
You think he cares enough about you
to get his shoes dirty?


01:08:29.391 --> 01:08:32.527
lf that were true, you wouldn't be here
with me in the first place.


01:08:32.624 --> 01:08:36.361
He's cheating on you, Ellie,
and everybody at school knows it but you.


01:08:37.958 --> 01:08:41.261
No, no, no, no.
Maybe he heard the gunshots.


01:08:41.357 --> 01:08:43.225
Or maybe, maybe he fired them.


01:08:43.324 --> 01:08:46.126
Why do you put him on such a pedestal?


01:08:46.224 --> 01:08:49.493
He doesn't give a rat's ass about you,
he told me so himself.


01:08:51.191 --> 01:08:53.092
He's not out looking for you.


01:08:53.191 --> 01:08:57.194
He's back at school, probably
in some freshman's dorm room right now.


01:08:57.624 --> 01:08:59.225
We got a camp a few miles away from here.


01:08:59.324 --> 01:09:01.693
We find the camp
and we can find our way home.


01:09:03.191 --> 01:09:05.893
No, no.
We've been turned around for an hour now.


01:09:05.991 --> 01:09:08.960
The only way we know
is towards the gunshots.


01:09:09.058 --> 01:09:14.663
Make your choice. Let someone who really
cares about you save you,


01:09:15.991 --> 01:09:18.993
or you can go crying to Brett like usual.


01:09:21.691 --> 01:09:25.327
No. Please, please don't leave me.


01:09:25.424 --> 01:09:28.326
You go in that direction
and you're walking alone.


01:09:28.424 --> 01:09:29.958
Please come with me.


01:09:31.691 --> 01:09:33.659
Aaron! Aaron.


01:09:58.858 --> 01:10:01.594
This is actually the most fun
l've had in quite a while.


01:10:02.891 --> 01:10:05.693
Some fun. l can't tell if l'm excited,


01:10:05.791 --> 01:10:07.726
or if l'm going to throw up in my mouth
from the terror.


01:10:10.925 --> 01:10:13.460
-Just in case it's the latter.
-All right.


01:10:18.724 --> 01:10:20.258
We don't even know
what the hell this thing is yet,


01:10:20.357 --> 01:10:23.393
and l'm already picking out
a spot on my wall for its head.


01:10:24.524 --> 01:10:28.194
You know what?
Maybe it's mutating and has two heads.


01:10:28.891 --> 01:10:31.093
lf that happens to be the case,
l get them both.


01:10:31.191 --> 01:10:33.059
lf there's three heads, you can have one.


01:10:33.157 --> 01:10:35.459
Guys, l can hear you. My girlfriend?


01:10:35.758 --> 01:10:38.861
You know, if he wants one of the heads,
l'm not giving him one of mine.


01:10:38.958 --> 01:10:40.292
He can't have mine neither.


01:10:40.391 --> 01:10:42.493
l didn't come out here to fight wild animals.


01:10:42.591 --> 01:10:46.194
Hey, hey, you know what? Look, we can't
find your girlfriend if we're all gator crap.


01:10:47.424 --> 01:10:52.028
Last chance, Brett. You gonna tell us
why you're stalking your own girlfriend?


01:10:52.124 --> 01:10:53.458
Wait a minute.


01:10:53.558 --> 01:10:56.594
lf this is about a restraining order,
there are ways around that.


01:10:56.691 --> 01:10:58.692
Believe me, l know.


01:10:58.925 --> 01:11:01.560
She's being lied to, about me.


01:11:03.825 --> 01:11:07.995
There's this guy, Aaron. He's a grad student.
He was tutoring her for a while.


01:11:08.124 --> 01:11:11.360
He told her there was another girl and
he used that opportunity to get between us.


01:11:11.458 --> 01:11:13.326
And now, he takes her with him on this trip


01:11:13.424 --> 01:11:14.892
and you can only guess
what he's hoping to do with her.


01:11:15.357 --> 01:11:16.691
l love it out here.


01:11:18.124 --> 01:11:19.859
Where's Dr. Phil when you need him?


01:11:23.825 --> 01:11:25.193
Who's Dr. Phil?


01:11:41.092 --> 01:11:42.259
lt's not her.


01:11:47.491 --> 01:11:48.625
Oh, my God. It's Tara.


01:11:48.724 --> 01:11:51.393
-Brett, get back.
-lt's her best friend. She must be close.


01:11:51.491 --> 01:11:55.027
We gotta find her. Ellie! Can you hear me?


01:11:55.124 --> 01:11:56.225
Shut up.


01:11:56.324 --> 01:11:57.892
Well, that's one way to bring them closer.


01:11:57.991 --> 01:11:59.659
Can you hear me?


01:11:59.758 --> 01:12:02.293
Shut up! Jonas, you ready for this?


01:12:04.124 --> 01:12:05.992
-Try not to mess up its head.
-Heads.


01:12:06.092 --> 01:12:07.226
Ellie!


01:12:31.758 --> 01:12:34.861
Man, that's gotta be the hottest thing
l've ever seen.


01:12:56.124 --> 01:12:57.091
Shit.


01:12:58.958 --> 01:13:00.225
He's awake.


01:13:04.291 --> 01:13:05.959
-All right, get Connor ready to run.
-Right.


01:13:15.357 --> 01:13:17.559
Need a bigger gun.
Definitely need a bigger gun.


01:13:18.991 --> 01:13:19.958
Wait!


01:13:21.058 --> 01:13:22.025
Stop!


01:14:21.991 --> 01:14:23.258
What was l thinking?


01:14:23.357 --> 01:14:24.891
Give me that.


01:14:27.291 --> 01:14:31.595
l'm afraid that l have to ban you
from ever participating


01:14:31.691 --> 01:14:35.061
in one of my hunting expeditions,
ever again.


01:14:35.157 --> 01:14:38.293
Something in the contract
about not blowing holes in the guide.


01:14:38.391 --> 01:14:40.593
No complaints from me.


01:14:40.691 --> 01:14:44.294
That bastard ruined my pants
and he stole my knife.


01:14:44.591 --> 01:14:46.793
Well, you stabbed him in the face.


01:14:47.357 --> 01:14:51.060
Yeah, l know. And l would have
carved my name in his hide


01:14:51.157 --> 01:14:52.992
had it not got stuck in his head.


01:14:53.424 --> 01:14:54.825
As for your bellyaching,


01:14:55.858 --> 01:14:58.994
it's not the first time
l've been shot by someone l know.


01:14:59.092 --> 01:15:01.427
God! It is the first time l've been hit.


01:15:08.991 --> 01:15:11.793
l'm afraid l'm not going to be able
to walk out of here.


01:15:16.925 --> 01:15:17.925
The boat.


01:15:19.858 --> 01:15:25.296
The boat? Yeah. Getting in the water
sounds like a fine idea to me, college boy.


01:15:25.524 --> 01:15:27.492
Well, unless you can think of another way.


01:15:27.591 --> 01:15:30.160
Actually, no, l can't.


01:15:30.858 --> 01:15:33.594
No way to keep our orientation
with the sun going down.


01:15:33.691 --> 01:15:36.393
When we get in the boat, where do we go?


01:15:37.025 --> 01:15:38.793
Only one place to go.


01:15:40.858 --> 01:15:43.727
There's a cabin on the other side of the lake.


01:15:45.157 --> 01:15:49.294
l'm having a bit of a misunderstanding
with the owner,


01:15:49.391 --> 01:15:54.829
so if anybody's there when we get there,
just keep the elk poaching on the down low.


01:16:00.291 --> 01:16:03.861
l'm the one with the injured leg,
Rambo, okay? Let's go.


01:16:03.958 --> 01:16:05.025
What about Ellie?


01:16:06.224 --> 01:16:09.694
We can't... We can't go looking for her now.
We wouldn't know where to look.


01:16:09.791 --> 01:16:13.094
-You think she's dead, don't you?
-l didn't say that.


01:16:14.025 --> 01:16:16.527
Look, l can't know for sure,


01:16:16.624 --> 01:16:19.793
but we wouldn't do her any good
if we get ourselves killed, would we?


01:16:19.891 --> 01:16:22.893
Those were crocodiles.
l've read enough about crocodiles


01:16:22.991 --> 01:16:25.893
to know they don't stop killing food
just because they're full.


01:16:26.324 --> 01:16:28.826
They also don't travel very far
if they don't have to. She's nearby.


01:16:28.925 --> 01:16:33.963
Whatever you do, do not start screaming
like you did the last time.


01:16:34.058 --> 01:16:35.759
She's my girlfriend!


01:16:35.858 --> 01:16:38.093
lf you had any kind of normal relationships,
you'd understand.


01:16:38.724 --> 01:16:40.025
Normal?


01:16:41.391 --> 01:16:47.663
Jonas and l chase
after a killer crocodile for you,


01:16:47.758 --> 01:16:50.060
practically playing 20 questions


01:16:50.157 --> 01:16:54.528
trying to figure out what would drive you
to follow Ellie in here to begin with.


01:16:54.624 --> 01:16:58.894
And may l point out that we didn't
even know the damsel's name


01:16:58.991 --> 01:17:02.260
until you start screaming it
at the top of your lungs,


01:17:02.357 --> 01:17:06.527
attracting that monster that came out
of the woods and bit off Jonas' head.


01:17:08.291 --> 01:17:11.761
And how the hell do you know
l don't have any normal relationships, huh?


01:17:11.858 --> 01:17:15.795
l know all about you.
All about your boo-hooing about Miss Ellie,


01:17:15.958 --> 01:17:19.294
but did you ask me one question,
one question about me and my life?


01:17:19.391 --> 01:17:20.525
Okay!


01:17:23.891 --> 01:17:24.891
Do you have a boyfriend?


01:17:27.691 --> 01:17:31.494
No. No, l don't have a boyfriend, dumbass.


01:17:32.357 --> 01:17:33.991
That was hypothetical.


01:17:35.058 --> 01:17:40.663
Now that you know all about me,
Iet's get in the boat and go someplace safe.


01:17:42.025 --> 01:17:43.259
No, l won't.


01:17:43.357 --> 01:17:45.025
-Really?
-Not without Ellie.


01:17:52.157 --> 01:17:55.493
Fine, we'll see how you like being dragged.


01:18:15.324 --> 01:18:17.759
-Johnny Law.
-Nathan, actually.


01:18:18.324 --> 01:18:21.360
l would have introduced myself last time,
but when l asked for your hunter's license


01:18:21.458 --> 01:18:23.326
you spit tobacco juice on my shoes.


01:18:23.424 --> 01:18:26.059
Yeah? l'm a shy girl.


01:18:27.758 --> 01:18:33.430
You know, you got a bit of an infestation
of a very unusual variety out there.


01:18:34.658 --> 01:18:36.493
Yeah, it looks like they got you pretty bad.


01:18:36.591 --> 01:18:39.060
There were four of us. And the other two


01:18:41.858 --> 01:18:46.195
didn't fare as well.


01:18:47.025 --> 01:18:48.693
But the crocs didn't shoot me.


01:18:51.524 --> 01:18:54.326
-That one did.
-l already said l was sorry.


01:18:56.157 --> 01:18:58.959
Thanks for taking us in,
but we need to get back out there.


01:18:59.058 --> 01:19:00.859
-l'm Brett, by the way.
-Nathan.


01:19:00.958 --> 01:19:02.592
Hey. Susan. This is Connor.


01:19:02.691 --> 01:19:04.626
Why would you wanna go back outside?
Are you crazy?


01:19:04.724 --> 01:19:06.992
Because my girlfriend's out there
on the lake.


01:19:07.458 --> 01:19:10.861
We were looking for her
when Reba decided to come here instead.


01:19:10.958 --> 01:19:14.561
lt's better off behind a closed door
than running around in the dark.


01:19:14.658 --> 01:19:17.427
Exactly why we need to get back on the boat
and find Ellie.


01:19:17.524 --> 01:19:18.725
We've been trapped in here for hours


01:19:18.825 --> 01:19:21.327
and there's the very real possibility
that help isn't coming.


01:19:21.424 --> 01:19:23.159
Now, we can't let you take
our only means of transportation


01:19:23.257 --> 01:19:24.291
and go and get yourself killed.


01:19:24.391 --> 01:19:27.694
Especially when that only means
of transportation belongs to me.


01:19:27.791 --> 01:19:31.494
We get back in the boat. We find Ellie,
and then we get the hell away from here.


01:19:31.591 --> 01:19:33.926
Ellie's on the lake.
Now we need to get to safety.


01:19:34.025 --> 01:19:35.493
That's connecting to the river
and going down to town.


01:19:35.591 --> 01:19:36.658
Those are opposite directions.


01:19:36.758 --> 01:19:39.160
No! This isn't up for debate.
We're not leaving her.


01:19:39.257 --> 01:19:41.459
We don't even know where she is.


01:19:41.558 --> 01:19:43.693
Now my wife and my son are right here
and l can't risk their lives


01:19:43.791 --> 01:19:45.792
based on the chance or the possibility
that she might be out there.


01:19:45.891 --> 01:19:48.893
Sensible conversation
didn't get me very far with her.


01:19:51.658 --> 01:19:52.859
l'm sorry to have to do this.


01:19:56.291 --> 01:19:58.526
l already shot someone today.
l don't mind doing it again.


01:19:58.624 --> 01:19:59.858
Get away from the door.


01:20:00.257 --> 01:20:02.492
Now's a fine time to grow yourself a pair.


01:20:06.858 --> 01:20:10.661
l will come back for you, promise.
Just as soon as l find her.


01:20:27.357 --> 01:20:28.424
Ellie!


01:20:36.958 --> 01:20:38.592
Ellie!


01:20:39.424 --> 01:20:40.491
Brett?


01:20:41.324 --> 01:20:43.359
Ellie!


01:20:48.025 --> 01:20:49.626
Ellie!


01:20:50.891 --> 01:20:52.125
Brett!


01:20:52.491 --> 01:20:53.992
Ellie!


01:20:54.658 --> 01:20:55.792
Brett!


01:21:02.357 --> 01:21:04.292
Be back sooner than l thought.


01:21:04.391 --> 01:21:06.493
Brett! Brett!


01:21:06.724 --> 01:21:08.025
l'm coming back!


01:21:08.157 --> 01:21:10.025
Brett, l'm here!


01:21:10.491 --> 01:21:11.892
Ellie!


01:21:11.991 --> 01:21:16.195
l'm here, baby. l'm here.
l knew. l knew. Brett!


01:21:21.324 --> 01:21:24.660
Connor, get in the bathroom
and lock the door. Go!


01:21:45.458 --> 01:21:46.559
Brett!


01:21:46.658 --> 01:21:47.692
No, no.


01:21:47.791 --> 01:21:50.026
Oh, my God. l knew. l knew.


01:21:50.124 --> 01:21:51.859
Move away from the water!


01:21:52.624 --> 01:21:53.691
What?


01:21:53.791 --> 01:21:57.995
Get away from the water!
Get away from the water!


01:22:24.891 --> 01:22:25.958
Ellie!


01:22:30.591 --> 01:22:31.925
Oh, my God!


01:22:42.958 --> 01:22:44.459
What is that?


01:22:50.257 --> 01:22:51.491
-l'm so sorry.
-Hey...


01:22:51.591 --> 01:22:53.426
Hey, hey. No. You don't need to apologize.


01:22:53.524 --> 01:22:56.293
-l'm sorry for going with him. With Aaron.
-Don't apologize. Don't.


01:22:56.391 --> 01:22:58.292
No. No, don't apologize.


01:23:02.324 --> 01:23:05.760
-l love you. l love you.
-l love you.


01:23:10.791 --> 01:23:13.927
Ellie, go. Go now. Go! Run! Now!


01:23:15.724 --> 01:23:18.860
Oh, my God. What is... What is that?


01:23:24.591 --> 01:23:25.792
Oh, my God!


01:23:49.758 --> 01:23:50.859
Nicely done.


01:23:51.092 --> 01:23:53.527
Let's get the hell out of here, now.


01:24:01.558 --> 01:24:04.894
That's okay.
l can always come back for the head later.


01:24:08.357 --> 01:24:10.025
Connor, stay close.


01:24:14.524 --> 01:24:16.158
Hey, hey, hey, hey.


01:24:17.424 --> 01:24:20.293
-Help me. It killed... It killed him.
-Who? Who?


01:24:20.391 --> 01:24:21.458
-Brett?
-Brett.


01:24:21.558 --> 01:24:24.861
-Get us in the boat, now!
-Right. Go! Go! Connor, come.


01:24:26.124 --> 01:24:27.792
-You okay?
-Yeah.


01:24:32.092 --> 01:24:33.326
Keep trying.


01:24:38.291 --> 01:24:40.359
Okay, plan B.


01:24:48.491 --> 01:24:49.725
Here we go.


01:24:51.424 --> 01:24:52.858
Yeah, l think we're safe.


01:24:53.891 --> 01:24:55.025
What is that?


01:24:58.825 --> 01:25:01.394
Go. Go. Go. Come on. Go.


01:25:08.092 --> 01:25:09.226
Got her?


01:25:12.058 --> 01:25:13.592
-Hello!
-Hello!


01:25:13.691 --> 01:25:14.725
Come on!


01:25:16.058 --> 01:25:17.159
Over there.


01:25:17.257 --> 01:25:20.360
What makes you think Dimitri's
not gonna have locked his doors?


01:25:28.058 --> 01:25:29.125
What now?


01:25:33.025 --> 01:25:34.059
After you.


01:25:42.658 --> 01:25:44.526
-Okay, let's put her down.
-l'll call for help.


01:25:44.624 --> 01:25:45.658
All right.


01:25:46.825 --> 01:25:48.960
-Does anybody have a quarter?
-No. No.


01:25:49.058 --> 01:25:51.527
-lt's 911, you don't need any money.
-Okay, okay.


01:26:04.391 --> 01:26:09.729
No, no, no, no, no. It's going to be okay.
We're gonna get out of here.


01:26:22.724 --> 01:26:26.828
What about Connor? This is all my fault.
l should have been there for him.


01:26:26.925 --> 01:26:28.026
This is my fault.


01:26:44.124 --> 01:26:48.595
lt's you. Little Bickerman! Don't you...


01:26:52.691 --> 01:26:55.326
Oh, my God! Run. Go, go, go!


01:27:32.624 --> 01:27:36.527
Help! Help! Help!


01:27:37.058 --> 01:27:38.325
Help!


01:27:42.891 --> 01:27:45.193
Help! Help!


01:28:10.758 --> 01:28:13.227
Connor! Susan! Backdoor's open. Go!


01:28:30.491 --> 01:28:31.491
No keys.


01:28:31.591 --> 01:28:34.093
-Don't you know how to hot-wire?
-l'm a zoologist.


01:28:34.858 --> 01:28:36.693
-Connor!
-Connor?


01:28:40.524 --> 01:28:41.591
Keys.


01:28:42.825 --> 01:28:45.994
This is the one and only time
you're allowed to steal something.


01:29:16.391 --> 01:29:18.292
Connor. Go.


01:29:34.458 --> 01:29:36.893
-Are we 07 or 08?
-07!


01:29:52.624 --> 01:29:53.958
Connor!


01:29:56.157 --> 01:29:57.925
Dad! Lighter!


01:30:18.291 --> 01:30:20.760
-Nate! Nate!
-No. Dad!


01:30:57.357 --> 01:31:00.993
l would like to present to you today
an absolutely extraordinary case,


01:31:01.524 --> 01:31:04.927
and proof that we are not in control.


01:31:06.624 --> 01:31:11.195
We're not in control of our jobs,
we're not in control of our children


01:31:12.491 --> 01:31:15.727
and we are certainly not in control
of this planet.


01:31:17.558 --> 01:31:19.893
There are no hard and fast rules in nature.


01:31:20.391 --> 01:31:25.162
There's no way to create a system
by which we can catalog and analyze


01:31:25.257 --> 01:31:27.926
and predict where an animal is gonna go


01:31:29.691 --> 01:31:32.193
or what an animal is gonna do.


01:31:33.025 --> 01:31:35.927
Having said all that,
l would like to now regale you


01:31:36.025 --> 01:31:41.663
with the story of a most unique species,
the Maine River Crocodile.


01:31:42.891 --> 01:31:45.727
For the record, it's extinct.


01:31:50.791 --> 01:31:51.858
Come along.


01:31:52.925 --> 01:31:57.195
So, did you guys have time
to read the pamphlets? Anyone?

